# CRYSTALLine

A desktop GUI for building/editing **CRYSTAL** structures and visualising
**vibrational (phonon) modes**, built on top of the
[CRYSTALClear](https://github.com/crystaldevs/CRYSTALClear) I/O + plotting
framework.

> Status: early scaffold (v0.0.1). The architecture is in place and the domain
> core is tested; the interactive 3D features are being built out.

## Architecture

The package is deliberately layered so domain logic stays independent of the Qt
UI (and therefore unit-testable without a display):

```
src/crystalline/
├── core/        domain model — Structure, PhononMode/PhononModes (no Qt)
├── crystalio/   thin adapter over CRYSTALClear (load .out/.gui, save .gui)
├── viz/         PyVista/VTK rendering + phonon animation (no Qt)
└── ui/          PySide6 widgets: viewport, dockable panels, main window
```

Only `ui/` (and the viewport that embeds the interactor) imports Qt. New
properties (DOS, bands, elastic surfaces, …) are added by dropping a new panel
into `ui/panels/` and wiring its signals in `MainWindow`.

## Setup

```sh
conda activate pypiero          # env created with PySide6 + pyvista + CRYSTALClear
pip install -e .                # editable install of crystalline
```

## Run

```sh
python -m crystalline
# or, after install:
crystalline
```

Use **File → Open structure** (`.out`/`.gui`) to load a geometry, or
**File → Open phonons** (`.out` from a frequency run) to load modes, then pick a
mode in the Phonons panel and press **Play**.

## Test

```sh
pytest        # exercises the Qt-free core (core/ + phonon math)
```

